evals.prompt:
Migrate this Express route to mint the realtime credential from ElevenLabs instead of OpenAI. Keep the route path and response shape the frontend expects.

```typescript
app.get("/api/token", async (_req, res) => {
  const r = await fetch("https://api.openai.com/v1/realtime/client_secrets", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
      Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY}`,
      "Content-Type": "application/json",
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      session: {
        type: "realtime",
        model: "gpt-realtime",
        instructions: "You are a cheerful concierge.",
        audio: { output: { voice: "marin" } },
      },
    }),
  });
  const data = await r.json();
  res.json({ value: data.value });
});
```

This React component talks to OpenAI Realtime over WebRTC. Port it to ElevenLabs Realtime, still using @openai/agents-realtime. The token comes from GET /api/token which now returns { value } minted by ElevenLabs.

```tsx
import { RealtimeAgent, RealtimeSession } from "@openai/agents-realtime";

export function Talk() {
  async function start() {
    const { value } = await fetch("/api/token").then((r) => r.json());
    const agent = new RealtimeAgent({ name: "Concierge", instructions: "You are a cheerful concierge." });
    const session = new RealtimeSession(agent, { model: "gpt-realtime" });
    await session.connect({ apiKey: value });
  }
  return <button onClick={start}>Talk</button>;
}
```

